{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And you shall give his inheritance to his kinsman who is close to him from his family.</b> From here the Rabbis, of blessed memory, drew support that the husband inherits his wife, and they would add and subtract words and expound: ונתתם את נחלת שארו לו — 'and you shall give the inheritance of his kinsman to him' — and 'his kinsman' (שארו) means his wife." "<b>And it shall be for the children of Israel a statute of judgment.</b> In the matter of inheritances Scripture mentions 'a statute of judgment' to indicate that this judgment of inheritances shall be a statute in Israel forever. And because one might think that the section of inheritances was given to apply only upon entry into the land and nothing more, therefore 'a statute of judgment' was necessary — that is, for the hour and for the generations." "<b>And the Rabbis, of blessed memory,</b> in Bava Batra learned from here, from the language of חקה, that a person cannot transfer by language of inheritance to one who is not fit to inherit him, nor uproot the inheritance from the heir — even though this is a monetary matter and whoever stipulates a condition contrary to what is written in the Torah, his condition stands in monetary matters, such as one who betroths a woman on condition that she has no claim upon him for food and clothing. But in the section of inheritances, in which חקת משפט is written, it comes to say that this statute shall not be changed and the condition is of no avail — whether the one making the stipulation was healthy or a dying man, whether orally or in writing, it is of no avail. Therefore one who says, 'So-and-so is my firstborn son — let him not take a double portion,' 'So-and-so is my son — let him not inherit with his brothers,' 'So-and-so who is not my son — let him inherit me' in a place where he has a daughter, 'My daughter — let her inherit me' in a place where he has a son, has said nothing; and likewise in all of them according to this order." "<b>As YHWH commanded.</b> It should have said, 'as I have commanded you,' since it is all the speech of the Holy One, blessed be He; but it is like (Exodus 24:1): ״ואל משה אמר עלה אל ה׳״ — 'and to Moshe He said: ascend to YHWH.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:32.322004363Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}